From e339656cdd1c9e09aaf1c4ca9a87c399e3df56a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brian Martin <brian.m.martin@oracle.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 16:32:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add an Emscripten/WebAssembly OS port for HotSpot Zero

Cross-compiles OpenJDK 21 Zero to WebAssembly with Emscripten.

  * autoconf learns the emscripten OS (VAR_OS_TYPE=unix), so
    src/hotspot/os/posix/* is reused unchanged - threading, semaphores
    and perf memory all come from the stock POSIX layer.
  * src/hotspot/os/emscripten/ and src/hotspot/os_cpu/emscripten_zero/
    are modelled on their bsd/bsd_zero counterparts. Only
    os_emscripten.cpp and os_emscripten_zero.cpp carry real logic; the
    rest are thin headers and stubs. src/hotspot/cpu/zero/* is untouched.
  * There is no dynamic loader, so os::dll_lookup resolves JNI entry
    points through a static name -> address table supplied by the
    embedder rather than dlsym(). imageDecompressor.cpp goes through
    JVM_FindLibraryEntry for the same reason - its dlsym() returned NULL
    and left ZipInflateFully null, trapping on every jimage read.
  * Emscripten's mmap emulation rejects a non-zero address, so reserve
    and commit collapse into a single mapping and mprotect/madvise are
    no-ops.
  * java.base natives build from share/ + unix/ only; there is no
    src/java.base/emscripten/. handleRead/handleAvailable gain an
    __EMSCRIPTEN__ branch that drains the embedder's SharedArrayBuffer
    stdin ring buffer, since nothing is on the other end of fd 0 in a
    browser tab.

Verified by booting the JVM in Node and in the browser, compiling and
running a class through the in-process CompileServer, and rendering
Mocha Doom to a canvas.
